                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 6,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Yesterday, the Federal Trade Commission published another report on the harmful impacts of the PBM industry. This new study shows what we already know \u2013 that PBMs have significantly drive up prescription drug prices, steer patients to their own pharmacies, artificially mark-up the costs of generics, and prevent patients from accessing care from their local independent pharmacy. This directly hurts Oklahomans, and I have been fighting against these practices for years. Grateful for the transparency the FTC reports bring, and I urge my colleagues to see this as a call to action. Take a look at the report here \u2b07\ufe0f\nhttps://t.co/MTscfsWXle",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
